1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,920
This is Hisaab. Private books for people who get paid in shielded

2
00:00:04,920 --> 00:00:05,342
Zcash.

3
00:00:06,350 --> 00:00:10,659
In India, every crypto payment has to show up in your tax return.

4
00:00:10,659 --> 00:00:15,033
But tax tools can't read shielded transactions, and wallet exports

5
00:00:15,033 --> 00:00:17,486
leave out what your accountant needs.

6
00:00:18,436 --> 00:00:20,630
Hisaab runs on your own machine.

7
00:00:20,630 --> 00:00:24,743
First, the freelancer connects an incoming-only viewing key.

8
00:00:24,743 --> 00:00:29,473
It can see money coming in, but it can't spend, and it can't see what

9
00:00:29,473 --> 00:00:31,392
you spend. Next, an invoice.

10
00:00:31,392 --> 00:00:35,985
The invoice code rides inside the encrypted memo of a Zcash payment

11
00:00:35,985 --> 00:00:39,893
link. Now the client pays from their own shielded wallet.

12
00:00:39,893 --> 00:00:43,252
This is a real transaction on the public testnet.

13
00:00:49,169 --> 00:00:52,192
Hisaab spots it in the mempool within seconds.

14
00:00:52,192 --> 00:00:54,425
We sped up the wait for the block.

15
00:00:56,103 --> 00:00:58,595
Mined, and matched to the invoice.

16
00:00:58,595 --> 00:01:01,527
One payment can only settle one invoice.

17
00:01:01,527 --> 00:01:06,219
Here's the ledger for the Indian financial year, April to March.

18
00:01:06,219 --> 00:01:11,057
And one click builds a pack for your CA: the ledger, a receipt for

19
00:01:11,057 --> 00:01:13,623
every payment, and a checksum file.

20
00:01:16,736 --> 00:01:21,296
Your CA checks it. Every file matches its checksum, every receipt

21
00:01:21,296 --> 00:01:25,856
matches the chain, and the wallet refused to spend with this key.

22
00:01:27,736 --> 00:01:31,207
Here's the same payment from the client's own wallet.

23
00:01:31,207 --> 00:01:33,040
Block height, time, and fee.

24
00:01:36,736 --> 00:01:40,082
On chain, amounts and memos stay private.

25
00:01:40,082 --> 00:01:43,264
Hisaab only ever holds a view-only key.

26
00:01:45,736 --> 00:01:49,311
Everything you just saw was real, on Zcash testnet.

27
00:01:49,311 --> 00:01:51,904
That's Hisaab. The code is on GitHub.
